    "narrative": "The analytical core of our lineup today centers on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest efficiency score of 76.16. He is locked into the two-hole against a vulnerable Paddack, providing an optimal base projection augmented by a 13% boost from the pitcher's projected performance. Close behind, **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.67) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) leverage high-ceiling matchups against Sugano and Severino, respectively. **Geraldo Perdomo** specifically benefits from an impressive 14% park-factor surge, while **Jung Hoo Lee** capitalizes on his premier spot at the top of the order, providing crucial table-setting value that aligns perfectly with our need for run production and high-volume plate appearances.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involved **Bryson Stott**, who hovered right at the edge of the starting threshold with a 54.06. Ultimately, **Bryson Stott** was edged out by **Lawrence Butler** and **Taylor Ward** due to the latter two's superior platoon advantages and higher dynamic positioning in their respective lineups. Despite a favorable matchup against Chandler, **Bryson Stott** suffered from a negative park factor and a low spot in the order, which, when coupled with the elite 1.89s pop time of the opposing catcher, constrained his upside relative to the rest of the outfield configuration. Meanwhile, **Gavin Sheets** was excluded entirely, falling below our 40-point efficiency floor due to an unfavorable matchup against the high-skill Gilbert.\n\nRisks remain focused on the lower end of our starting rotation, particularly regarding **Lawrence Butler**, who draws a tough assignment against McDonald (2.87 xERA). While his dynamic platoon edge of 13% keeps him viable, the sub-3.00 xERA of the opposing starter introduces significant volatility to his performance. We are closely monitoring weather and late lineup changes, but as it stands, the combination of **Luis Arraez** and **Jonathan Aranda** provides a solid floor, leveraging a collective 26% boost in SP skill-matchup favorability to offset any potential early-game stagnation. **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Daulton Varsho** are expected to hold steady, though we remain vigilant on the defensive metrics that might limit stolen base opportunities across the slate.",
